@startuml keeper-team-start
!theme plain
title Keeper start with its standing team (v1.3): every autonomous agent is an OS user; identities come from the key keeper; bring-up is idempotent after a reboot

actor "Owner" as OW
participant "Registry / keeper\n(S4: binding, team[], up)" as Reg
participant "Launch dispatcher" as D
participant "Privileged helper\n(sudo: users, homes, firewall)" as PH
participant "Key keeper\n(master secret, derivation)" as KK
participant "Launcher\n(curator run)" as L
participant "Session host" as SH
participant "Bridge\n(broker, mailbox)" as BR
participant "Keeper session\n(OS user keeper_x)" as K

== reboot or first start ==
Reg -> Reg: boot_id changed; read team[] of product X:\n{role, identity, standing|ephemeral, max}
Reg -> D: bring up standing members (idempotent)
loop for each standing member (keeper first, then orchestrators)
  D -> PH: ensure user <identity>: private home, mode 0700,\nno parent ACL, group, firewall rules for the UID
  PH --> D: uid, home (no change if it already exists)
  D -> KK: register(uid, identity path product/project/agent')
  KK -> KK: derive public key for the path;\nroot signature "descendant N" published once
  KK --> D: public key, registry record (unchanged if known)
  D -> L: launch as <identity> (profile, expect_pin, binding)
  L -> SH: intake (plan, pin, binding pin)
  SH -> K: exec under a holder as the OS user; closed fence
  L -> BR: bind I/O (rooms of product X), mailbox for the identity
  SH -> SH: issue session token; readiness probe; fence open
  SH --> D: RUN record {identity, uid, execution}
end
D --> Reg: team up; standing slots ready

== later: an ephemeral worker ==
K -> D: dispatch(LaunchRequest{role developer, ephemeral})
note right of D: see spawn-with-user: new user, new key,\nremoved at retire
@enduml
